  <p>UDOT says the final decision on these walls will not be made until design is complete and refined utility relocation and right-of-way costs are known; reasonableness will be rechecked with those costs before balloting.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %} The noise study did not model the planned 4000 South interchange, because of anticipated construction phasing; it analyzed a tie-in at 4000 South instead and says the interchange will be reanalyzed in a future phase.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-appendix-nov2026" %} Residents near 4000 South should watch for that later analysis.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>Sound wall precedent (Phase 2 Davis County):</strong> The noise wall balloting process for the Phase 2 extension produced approved walls at multiple locations, establishing a strong local precedent for mitigation at similar distances. All three walls that went to ballot were approved.{% cite "udot-wdc-phase2-noise" %}</p>
  </div>

